1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,373
Fourteen ships entered the

2
00:00:01,393 --> 00:00:03,514
Suez Canal for a one-day trip.

3
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:05,220
They got out eight years later.

4
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:07,420
Halfway through, war broke out.

5
00:00:07,440 --> 00:00:09,353
Egypt sank ships to block the canal.

6
00:00:09,373 --> 00:00:11,820
And the canal became the front line.

7
00:00:11,870 --> 00:00:13,895
Trapped in a lake, nowhere to go.

8
00:00:13,915 --> 00:00:15,844
Sandstorms dusted them yellow.

9
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:17,030
The Yellow Fleet.

10
00:00:17,070 --> 00:00:18,560
Their countries were rivals.

11
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:20,230
The sailors became friends.

12
00:00:20,250 --> 00:00:21,340
Football on deck.

13
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:22,375
Their own stamps.

14
00:00:22,520 --> 00:00:23,730
Their own Olympics.

15
00:00:23,830 --> 00:00:24,511
Poland won.

16
00:00:24,531 --> 00:00:27,040
In the end, just two could still sail.

17
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:28,180
Home to Hamburg.

18
00:00:28,290 --> 00:00:30,083
Tens of thousands cheered.

19
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:31,080
Part of the cargo?

20
00:00:31,210 --> 00:00:32,017
Kitchen clocks.

21
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:33,880
Delivered only eight years late.

22
00:00:34,150 --> 00:00:35,830
How many stars for this delivery?
